<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile.xml                       FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_PRISON_1

  The prison tank's occupant/escapee — "one species at two scales, exactly
  the dianoga's own relation: the tank holds a juvenile, and the adult is
  the thing below the Fever Wood" (item, "tier — and the free-tier occupant
  is the SEKKULAATH"). The adult itself is deliberately never a Pawn
  (FEVERWOOD_TENTACLE_BESTIARY_1: only tentacles, modelled as stationary
  Buildings, are ever drawn) — this is the ONLY renderable, tameable form
  the species has, which is exactly what a display-tank captive needs to
  be.

  Franchise-free RM tier (Q11a) — this def must not reference anything
  Star Wars. The campaign-layer swap ("Swap[s] the Dianoga in, replacing the
  Sekkulaath, when RimMandrake.StarWars is present", owner verbatim) is a
  PatchOperationReplace shipped from the OTHER side instead:
  src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Patches/RSW_SekkulaathTank_DianogaSwap.xml,
  MayRequire="mandrake.rm.feverwood", retargets
  RM_CompProperties_CapturedSpecimen.occupantKindDefName on the tank's own
  ThingDef from RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile to RSW_Dianoga — so this def never
  needs to know Star Wars content exists, and the swap is genuinely "swap,
  not add" (one def-slot, never both).

  Body: "Snake" (vanilla Core BodyDef) — verified in-repo use, not guessed;
  every RM_/RSW_ small aquatic/serpentine creature already shipped in this
  codebase uses it (RM_PropaneLakeFauna, RM_ScaldFauna, RM_TwilightSeaFauna,
  RM_GreySeaFauna, RM_StockedPoolFauna). Not tentacle-accurate at the
  body-part level, but body parts here only gate damage/health, not the
  sprite — the actual silhouette is the texture, flagged placeholder below.

  Ruling 3 (owner, 2026-09-23), verbatim: "It should have advanced training,
  but you would have to train it by releasing it from the tanks... Advanced
  training is fine, but it should have large wildness, be very challenging
  to tame, and have a high chance of attacking if you fail." trainability
  Advanced is the ruled value; Wildness/manhunterOnTameFailChance/
  manhunterOnDamageChance below are INVENTED placeholders standing in for
  numbers the owner explicitly said not to guess — see
  FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_TANK_TUNING_1 for the real pass. waterSeeker=true is the
  built-in vanilla lever for "makes for the nearest water" (§6m stage 1);
  it is an approximation (a race flag, not a custom beeline JobGiver) and is
  documented as such in that item.

  specificMeatDef repoints to RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh (already shipped by
  FEVERWOOD_TENTACLE_BESTIARY_1) rather than a new meat resource — the same
  "renewable source of the animal's body" the severed-limb harvest already
  is, so a butchered escapee and a fed tank's meat output are one material,
  not two.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: one flat-color 128x128 PNG (Graphic_Single, not the usual
  3-directional Graphic_Multi — a deliberate scope cut to avoid three
  placeholder files for a creature real art will replace outright), deep
  purple per the canon-confirmed colour ruling ("deep purple skin",
  FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_PRISON_1). Searched infrastructure/artpipe/done +
  registry.jsonl for "sekkulaath"/"dianoga" first (standing rule) — found
  canon_dianoga_v1_* (the SEPARATE Star Wars-tier art, not reusable here per
  Q11a) and nothing for a franchise-free juvenile. Real bespoke art is owed.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</defName>
    <label>sekkulaath</label>
    <description>A small, dark, tentacled thing, kept in tanks because nothing else keeps it. It is not the elder being beneath the Fever Wood's pools — not yet — but it is unmistakably kin to it, and everyone who has heard it hum up close swears they will never mistake the sound again.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.6</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>420</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>5</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>60</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.08</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <FilthRate>10</FilthRate>
      <!-- INVENTED placeholder — owner ruled "large", not a number. -->
      <Wildness>0.85</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>tentacle</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>14</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FeverWood.RM_CompProperties_EscapedCaptive" />
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>Snake</body>
      <baseBodySize>0.9</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>1.1</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.8</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal, OmnivoreAnimal, AnimalProduct</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <specificMeatDef>RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh</specificMeatDef>
      <bloodDef>Filth_Slime</bloodDef>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Light</leatherDef>
      <trainability>Advanced</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>8</lifeExpectancy>
      <!-- INVENTED placeholders — direction ruled (owner: "very
           challenging to tame", "high chance of attacking if you fail"),
           values not. FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_TANK_TUNING_1. -->
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.55</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.85</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <waterSeeker>true</waterSeeker>
      <waterCellCost>1</waterCellCost>
      <gestationPeriodDays>10</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.5, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.15</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
          <soundCall>Pawn_Cobra_Call</soundCall>
          <soundWounded>Pawn_Cobra_Wounded</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>Pawn_Cobra_Death</soundDeath>
          <soundAngry>Pawn_Cobra_Call</soundAngry>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Reptile_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</defName>
    <label>sekkulaath</label>
    <race>RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</race>
    <combatPower>60</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0</ecoSystemWeight>
    <!-- ecoSystemWeight 0: never a wild-roster spawn (RM_FeverWood's own
         <wildAnimals> does not carry this def) — the only ways one exists
         are the tank's initial occupant and Escape(). -->
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <label>sekkulaath hatchling</label>
        <labelPlural>sekkulaath hatchlings</labelPlural>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.8</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile/RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.1</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
